# 5-page sample-female preview PDF

Separate from the **2026 program report** (12-page `burn-and-build-diet-kristi-*.pdf`). Sample-female: Welcome → Lean Body Analysis → Food Plan → Servings → Food List (×2).

When the user asks for **5-page**, **sample-female**, or **bb-five-page** PDF work, use this pipeline — not `render:program-report-preview`.

## Pipeline

| Piece | Path |
|-------|------|
| Renderer | `server/pdf/renderFivePagePrintout.js` |
| Frame / header | `server/pdf/draw1982Frame.js` |
| Food list pages | `server/pdf/drawStaplesFoodListPages.js` |
| Payload | `js/fivePagePrintoutData.js` → `buildKristiFivePagePreviewPayload()` |
| Copy | `js/fivePagePrintoutCopyData.js` |
| Render script | `scripts/render-five-page-preview.mjs` |
| Sample file | `docs/samples/bb-five-page-sample-female-N.pdf` (N auto-increments) |

Run: `npm run render:five-page-preview`

## Delivery order (critical — tell the user)

The download link is a **raw GitHub URL**. It serves whatever is **committed on `main`**, not what was just rendered locally.

**Required order every time:**

1. Edit renderer / payload / copy
2. `npm run render:five-page-preview`
3. **Commit** the new `bb-five-page-sample-female-N.pdf` (and code changes)
4. **`git push origin main`**
5. **Only then** paste the download link for **that numbered file**

If you give the link **before push**, the user gets the **previous** PDF in Mac **Downloads** — wrong size, wrong page count, or missing fixes. Say explicitly: *“Pushed to main — tap this link; it will save to Downloads.”*

## Give the user (one link only)

```
https://raw.githubusercontent.com/koryedwards-del/landing-burn-and-build/main/docs/samples/bb-five-page-sample-female-<N>.pdf
```

- **One** new numbered file per render (e.g. `bb-five-page-sample-female-12.pdf`) — each tap saves a unique name in **Mac Downloads** (no `-latest-2` suffix clutter).
- State the exact filename in the message.
- Do not also send `-latest`, archive, or program-report links for sample-female work.

## Do not

| Wrong | Why |
|-------|-----|
| Link before push | GitHub still serves old bytes |
| `render:program-report-preview` for sample-female | Wrong product (12+ pages) |
| Multiple download links per change | Clutters Downloads; confuses which file is current |
| Cursor artifacts panel | Broken download UX on Cursor Web |
| `github.com/.../blob/...` | Opens browser; does not download |

## Sanity check after render

Current sample-female should be **6 pages** minimum (~90 KB+ with food lists), Times fonts, full header every page. If ~50 KB or 4 pages only, food lists are missing. If ~180 KB or 13+ pages, the wrong renderer was used.
